 - **Cache once per session precomputed** Sevopedia Traits' Charts and Sevopedia Improvements' Weights (Leaders) Chart on category open before any entry is clicked on. This uses a simplified version of the AI Personality Panel's caching approach. See [AI Personality panel caching](/_1_AdvCiv-SAS/Docs/README_AI_Personality_Panel.md#notes-about-performance-optimization-of-the-ai-personality-panel-caching).
 - **Load Precomputed Files**: optionally load the Sevopedia Leader's **AI Personality Panel**'s information to display as a **predumped** file ([SevoPediaLeaderCachePredumped.py](/Assets/Python/Contrib/Sevopedia/SevoPediaLeaderCachePredumped.py)): (~550k Python literal characters) (default ON, recommended): since these values never change for players, this is more efficient. For modders, if they change leader XML info values, they can turn the SAS define to always compute temporarily so they can regenerate then update the file, or permanently for quick testing or if they prefer.
 - **External File Opening**: Access from Civ4 ingame local files in the system on Windows. See [KI#87](/_1_AdvCiv-SAS/Docs/README_Known_Issues.md#87---fixed-and-generalized-cannot-open-bug-mod-help-engchm-on-windows-in-advciv-sas-but-can-open-it-on-windows-in-base-advciv-even-though-path-is-the-same)
+- (Requires AdvCiv-SAS 5754+) Refactor to **helper files** reusable logic; e.g., debug dropdown making and place legend link or geometry for advisors [SASUtils.py](/Assets/Python/SASUtils.py); expanded text and animation panels or draw none text ([_sevopedia_helpers.py](/Assets/Python/Contrib/Sevopedia/_sevopedia_helpers.py)), and many others.
 - Make **paths absolute** in **.gitignore** to fix folders with an identical name being incorrectly ignored; add **.gitattributes** for more precise archiving.
 - Fix/cleanup **incorrect char formatting**: e.g.; `"Berang�r"` -> `"Beranger"`; removed non-English hints.
 - Consolidated **long, unneeded, or unused comments** into [Long_Comments/](/Long_Comments/) and replaced them with short custom markers or files to keep code clean, lean, and readable. > ~500k characters reduced and still ongoing.
@@ -345,8 +346,9 @@ Note: New panels added or modified mostly not mentioned here for concision. See
 - (Requires AdvCiv-SAS 5531+) **Beautified** and **expanded**, and add **support for text upscaling** for miscallenous **screens**: [CvDawnOfMan.py](/Assets/Python/Screens/CvDawnOfMan.py) ("The sun rises on the Year" greeting new game screen) is **expanded laterally and vertically** to **avoid scrolling**, add **icons** for buildings and units, add icon **chars for traits**; [CvTechSplashScreen.py](/Assets/Python/Screens/CvTechSplashScreen.py) (when a new tech is discovered)  is moderately **expanded** to **avoid scrolling**, vertically center screen (was slightly excentered); [CvHallOfFameScreen.py](/Assets/Python/Screens/CvHallOfFameScreen.py) is **maximized to full screen** with enlarged columns, and **new Leader, Civilization, Player Color, and Traits columns** with **icons** or **colors** or **chars** (based on Info Screen's Score tab: note that Civilization icon is approximative and will not work if Civilization name is not the base civ mod name (e.g. "The United States" -> "My American Custom Name Empire") (would add too much complexity in DLL for a working UI feature outside this edge case); note 2: trait info is indicative only (if traits in XML were different when the save file was made (e.g., expansive trait removed, leader trait allocation changed), this information will be lost)); [CvReplayScreen.py](/Assets/Python/Screens/CvReplayScreen.py) is **maximized to full screen**; [CvDanQuayle.py](/Assets/Python/Screens/CvDanQuayle.py) ("you have displayed the leadership abilities" post-game screen) is **maximized to full screen** and has a **greatly expanded leader NIF** and **maximized vertically score table** to **avoid scrolling**. See [README.md (Miscallenous screens)](/README.md#miscallenous-screens)
 - (Requires AdvCiv-SAS 5517+) **Reorganized advisors**: **merged** the **espionage** screen into the **Foreign Advisor**, the **Economic Advisor's Finance Tab** into the **Domestic Advisor**, moved away the **Environment Tab** from the former **Economic Advisor** (now removed), the **Religion** Advisor and **Corporation** Advisor (so it is always visible and easier to access) into the new **Policy Advisor**; so they are now **tabs of these instead** (deleted the old now obsolete lone advisor .py files); **swap advisors**: **Victory screen** to F9 and **Info Screen** to F8 so the Info Screen is easier to split to F7 and F8 later on and so layout is **more logically organized** from internal to external advisors; **split advisors**: the **Foreign Advisor** is now split into **Foreign Trade Advisor (F4)** (TREATIES, BONUSES, TECHS, CITIES), and **Foreign Diplomacy Advisor (F3)** (RELATIONS, GLANCE, INFO, ESPIONAGE) as it **was crowded** to reduce the need for **tab navigation** and for **clearer thematic differentiation**, using a shell (i.e. almost empty file for **linking only**) [CvForeignDiplomacyAdvisor.py](/Assets/Python/Screens/CvForeignDiplomacyAdvisor.py) file for the 2nd advisor.
 - (Requires AdvCiv-SAS 5524+) Rearrange Advisor **keyboard shortcuts** (in [CIV4ControlInfos.xml](/Assets/XML/Units/CIV4ControlInfos.xml) and DLL files like [CvEnums.h](/CvGameCoreDLL/CvEnums.h), [CvEnums.h](/CvGameCoreDLL/CvEnums.h), [CvGameInterface.cpp](/CvGameCoreDLL/CvGameInterface.cpp), and [CyEnumsInterface.cpp](/CvGameCoreDLL/CyEnumsInterface.cpp)) and adjust the **order of advisor buttons** in map view and **Sevopedia shortcuts** corresponding text to match the advisors changes.
+- (Requires AdvCiv-SAS 5754+) Add **debug mode support** (for player selection) in the Domestic Advisor. Add **Barbarian** to **selectable leaders** in debug mode in advisors where it is relevant: Domestic Advisor, Policy Advisor, World Advisor, and Info Screen.
 - (Requires AdvCiv-SAS 5521+) **Expand** and most **advisors** so they scale to **game resolution dynamically** instead of hardcoded advisor screen dimensions. The code was also refactored to improve **dynamic scaling**, ensuring **most UI elements automatically realign** if dimensions are changed. Advisors are now **excentered** so **overall more information** is displayed, thus **reducing the need for scrolling**, while still **preserving key relevant information** for display (scoreboard, map, commerce sliders and values, etc.). Some of their dimensions are **harmonized**. Note: some **right space for scoreboard** and **top space for the top bars** of the main interface was made (since commerce sliders are now as of now on the right side, they don't need left space anymore). See [Main Advisors reworks](/README.md#main-advisors-reworks-eg-overview-tabs-domestic-advisor-new-world-advisor-score-tab-and-timeline-tab-info-screen).
-- **Beautified** the **Domestic Advisor**: now shows the **button (i.e. icon) of the current item being built** (unit, building, project, process) in "Producing" column. (Requires AdvCiv-SAS 5522+) Use the **shared advisor shell layout** (**top/bottom bars** + single content panel, remove the old exit icon) so Domestic Advisor **mirrors other advisors' structure** instead of a floating table, now using a **clearer constrast dark yellow theme** instead, (Requires AdvCiv-SAS 5753+) and is now has **tabs**; **enhanced** the Domestic Advisor so it now has **4 overview tabs** with detailed city information (modifiers, yields, specialists, etc.) with a corresponding **legend link**, and an **enter city on click button** (mirroring the info screen's wonders tab). Added **debug mode support** (for player selection). Change in [CvDomesticAdvisor.py](/Assets/Python/Screens/CvDomesticAdvisor.py).
+- **Beautified** the **Domestic Advisor**: now shows the **button (i.e. icon) of the current item being built** (unit, building, project, process) in "Producing" column. (Requires AdvCiv-SAS 5522+) Use the **shared advisor shell layout** (**top/bottom bars** + single content panel, remove the old exit icon) so Domestic Advisor **mirrors other advisors' structure** instead of a floating table, now using a **clearer constrast dark yellow theme** instead, (Requires AdvCiv-SAS 5753+) and is now has **tabs**; **enhanced** the Domestic Advisor so it now has **4 overview tabs** with detailed city information (modifiers, yields, specialists, etc.) with a corresponding **legend link**, and an **enter city on click button** (mirroring the info screen's wonders tab). Change in [CvDomesticAdvisor.py](/Assets/Python/Screens/CvDomesticAdvisor.py).
 - (Requires AdvCiv-SAS 5528+) Minor **beautified** the [CvCustomizableDomesticAdvisor.py](/Assets/Python/Screens/CvCustomizableDomesticAdvisor.py): increase **legend culture text width** so it is not cramped when upscaled. Note: although it is functional, the Custom Domestic Advisor is **not supported** in AdvCiv-SAS as of now, so it is lacking the Finance Tab. See also [KI#123](/_1_AdvCiv-SAS/Docs/README_Known_Issues.md#123---fixed-bug-domesticmilitary-advisor-variant-toggles-required-restarting-civ4).
 - (Requires AdvCiv-SAS 5522+) New **Policy Advisor**. **Beautified**: enlarge **top panels text** so **long civic names don't overflow**. **Remove multiline nationality** information which was **uninfomative** and **crowded vertically** in the **Religions tab** and the **Corporations tab**; use more precise and compact `Leader (ID)` and `HQ (ID)` **one-liner instead** (**ID** also handles **one leader name being used by several players**); **increase row spacing** (now **unified** (was crowded)). **Remove multiline wrapped bonuses** splitting logic in the **Corporations tab**: use one natural comma-separated line (bonuses row height reduced/standardized) since there is enough space after expanding the Policy Advisor and it is more readable. Also add **new rows** (**Bonuses Generated**, **Yields Generated**), and add **first column descriptions** for rows (as of now `Built By:`, `Consumes:`, `Generates:`, `Generates 2:`). Add a **Great Person icon** in `Built By:` row. Change in [CvPolicyAdvisorScreen.py](/Assets/Python/Screens/CvPolicyAdvisorScreen.py).
 - **Foreign Advisor**: refined its tabs so they can display **up to 12 players**. Notably renamed the Active tab to **Treaties** tab (no longer shows redundant bonuses (since their deal can be cancelled from the bonuses tab)), and **beautified** it with **icons**. (Requires AdvCiv-SAS 5516+) Always use the unified **table-style info layout** (`drawInfoImproved`) for the Info Tab for stable column behavior: the old hardcoded text spacing (`drawInfoOriginal`) did not **scale with upscaled font text** nor **adjust depending on advisor screen size**. Plus the improved layout has additional **information** like general or specific **colored leader attitude text** related to civic/religion choices (e.g., `[-2]` or `[+1]`). (Requires AdvCiv-SAS 5518+) **Beautified** the **Espionage Tab** similarly; notably **removed redundant Espionage slider** now that commerce sliders are on the right side of main interface in map view, and **improved text spacing** that **was colliding or overflowing** beyond its panel, and **moved + - buttons under the leader icon** where there is more room and it is more intuitive and easier to click it.

